[{:db/id "q-74637/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b9e5c17d-c522-5bf6-8f70-d3d8c9e62496" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74637/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d90014dd-8f5a-59f1-a5f7-f75e440cbc9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74637/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "0d4cb1c2-0f40-5811-88fb-aa0f03d56b6f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74637/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ba8ee8eb-aa7e-55c2-a2e1-2224b9f05708" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74637/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "349da84b-7ff2-511f-b618-6127a020a1c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74637/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "51acfc1c-b2bd-529c-b7b2-121a3a3c2a04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74637/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-74637/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-74637/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-74637/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-74637/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-74637/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74637" :question/id #uuid "73568627-ecb4-569e-a7bc-c419d4ec5caa" :question/math-academy-id "q-74637" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=-1 \\\\  & x-2y=1 \\\\  & -x-5y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 7y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-\\frac{3}{7}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{3}{7})=1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \nSo, we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74637/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "22a357c1-7549-55d0-ad6d-9141712f9e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d54ab007-714c-5a9c-84af-d5a2dd327ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "3296df0a-ea13-58c3-b4b4-99a6685fcf76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d0021394-a89e-5ebb-8236-a161122bb775" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d1b6cc27-4d7c-5ca6-9d4d-ebc460989c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd126e4-c10e-5108-9768-666ca8740367" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74643/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-74643/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-74643/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-74643/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-74643/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-74643/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74643" :question/id #uuid "35b0295d-1e16-59cc-a201-696e791e0b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74643" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=8 \\\\  & x+y=-2 \\\\  & x+\\frac{1}{2}y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y=-2 \\\\ -y=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695/selection/b5a1b0c45c4c4694323b97d97aeacef1dd80693e5a018acc43f6a1b42bd7b8d5" :answer/id #uuid "7f30d341-6da0-522d-a671-0cafd55156ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695/selection/137501af3ee859ebc04c1ab0d44d1b8c87d2d9c5abf6c7a5030f36ed2b1cd52b" :answer/id #uuid "d8792715-b6bc-5a1b-92c0-e4cb61d759ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695/selection/5d0b1b60997252903d0e6a1fcb339952d330ce702af71d82f82759d29f64510d" :answer/id #uuid "8d115cde-602a-54d5-9461-91a8d8f63451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" :answer/id #uuid "c8a1bd78-0d0b-560c-aeae-749b98a53c02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695/selection/fb81972cd2e8e5796bcf653555c40038f71f47e65b0eb7fa3096c87bc0407fc8" :answer/id #uuid "2ce0a6e1-1cd9-5303-b46e-e6fb1716b9dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7dc0d21c-0475-51ab-8971-e71d3b3d8b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74695/selection/137501af3ee859ebc04c1ab0d44d1b8c87d2d9c5abf6c7a5030f36ed2b1cd52b" :answer-field/choices ["q-74695/selection/b5a1b0c45c4c4694323b97d97aeacef1dd80693e5a018acc43f6a1b42bd7b8d5" "q-74695/selection/137501af3ee859ebc04c1ab0d44d1b8c87d2d9c5abf6c7a5030f36ed2b1cd52b" "q-74695/selection/5d0b1b60997252903d0e6a1fcb339952d330ce702af71d82f82759d29f64510d" "q-74695/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" "q-74695/selection/fb81972cd2e8e5796bcf653555c40038f71f47e65b0eb7fa3096c87bc0407fc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74695" :question/id #uuid "0c4e1d34-2525-5325-9cac-3c34960d43c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74695" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 4x+2y=-8 \\\\  & x+ky=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & k & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & k & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2-4k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=2 \\\\  & (2-4k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{1}{2},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=2.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74695/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c9ac3733-0d0e-5a88-b345-329bd6cb3b04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "aaf338cd-9286-5668-b852-eb2386c3fa19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8e92264a-a4fc-5a19-bbcb-5be08b9cc62f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "83bf2a12-39a2-5602-b05e-ba0c45534298" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "9c7be0b7-6b55-5a17-80fe-d7bc93a328d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0d2e636-2be6-5efb-8cab-d1be95194167" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131721/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-131721/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-131721/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-131721/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131721/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-131721/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131721" :question/id #uuid "b9b47374-5548-52b6-9b51-17d923fcd37b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131721" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+7y=1 \\\\  & -2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131721/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131721"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" :answer/id #uuid "3c081651-1a19-5925-9b99-468f503ac540" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726/selection/9ef3fe6143bf6e314cf425f48243d909b1a6ae7f448cf381d5e01d056077662f" :answer/id #uuid "1d220542-f621-5f08-9dea-39d838c3580e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726/selection/ad168d067f7536455383404a1d3faefe3db3b1e330a36e3c216c85c81fdf87a8" :answer/id #uuid "d789a5ad-7781-5e4e-b4d9-9d1c30672834" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726/selection/c2e9cbc73ddec801b64583fc77a4e7b9468b8a554c6e72ecc582c1c34171bc66" :answer/id #uuid "ef0f692d-b6a3-5da1-a786-6d63238ecf6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726/selection/99cf9aaf76e0fbfe0a44a681275eb0801b5ea619cac36b3ef641b833f1cadf5f" :answer/id #uuid "f2955b31-5342-5792-b856-f0dd66a79f7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57b4cd74-0850-56ed-9a42-fcffd5867fee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131726/selection/c2e9cbc73ddec801b64583fc77a4e7b9468b8a554c6e72ecc582c1c34171bc66" :answer-field/choices ["q-131726/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" "q-131726/selection/9ef3fe6143bf6e314cf425f48243d909b1a6ae7f448cf381d5e01d056077662f" "q-131726/selection/ad168d067f7536455383404a1d3faefe3db3b1e330a36e3c216c85c81fdf87a8" "q-131726/selection/c2e9cbc73ddec801b64583fc77a4e7b9468b8a554c6e72ecc582c1c34171bc66" "q-131726/selection/99cf9aaf76e0fbfe0a44a681275eb0801b5ea619cac36b3ef641b833f1cadf5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131726" :question/id #uuid "0e33178a-23c0-59ca-9bb0-c57d74cec44d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131726" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -3x+2y=1 \\\\  & 6x+(k+9)y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+9 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+9 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+13 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y=1 \\\\ (k+13)y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-13,$ then the second equation is $0=7,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-13.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131726/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131726"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
